ulative)\n- Risking chips on a pure bluff with nothing is unnecessary\n\nReason:\nI should check and see the showdown. My opponent has checked through all streets, suggesting weakness. While my Ace-high is very weak, checking costs me nothing and gives me a chance to win at showdown if my opponent also has nothing or a weaker high card. Bluffing would risk chips unnecessarily when I can see showdown for free. Given I'm ahead in the match, preserving chips and avoiding unnecessary risk is the optimal strategy.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
